      "message": "Since host C++ utilities in `platform/ec` build with `-std\u003dgnu++23` and `-fno-exceptions`, please use `std::expected` for fallible operations across this stack (similar to `util/elan/`, `util/egis/`, and `util/focaltech/`).\n\nAt the `RtsUsbBackend` seam, using `std::expected\u003c..., int\u003e` (where the error is the negative `libusb_error` code) avoids losing error details:\n- `open()` currently returns `bool`, which discards `LIBUSB_ERROR_ACCESS` vs. `LIBUSB_ERROR_NO_DEVICE` — returning `std::expected\u003cvoid, int\u003e` lets callers fail immediately on permission errors instead of reporting \"device not found\" or polling until timeout.\n- `init()` can similarly return `std::expected\u003cvoid, int\u003e` for consistency.",
